first on cbs mornings we're joined by  the head coach of the newly named did  you hear it the washington drum roll  please commanders  yeah ron rivera is a head coach the nfl  franchise made the announcement just a  short time ago and this is what the  team's new helmet will look like this is  very cool looking  i like it i like the colors it says  commanders right there in front in 2020  you know the franchise [ __ ] its  longtime name of the redskins many  native american groups as you know said  that that name was hurtful and a  dictionary defined racial slur it's been  known as a washington football team ever  since until today head coach ron rivera  joins us to take us behind the scenes  hey coach rivera we're so excited that  you're here good to see you  really good to see you it's good to see  you gail thank you  so you know you guys had a lot of names  to choose from i know i had nothing at  all to do with this decision you consult  with me about nothing  and so but this was absolutely my first  choice so take us behind the scenes you  had a lot to consider why did you and  your team associated with this  making this decision decide commanders  was the way to go  you know working with the snyders and  with jason for the most part you know we  had got over 30 000 you know people  sending in uh names and trying to get us  to go in their direction and it was very  interesting because you went through it  there were a lot of good possibilities  but there are also other reasons behind  not being able to choose those other  names so when we started going through  the list and they started to bring it  down to a final grouping  the commander stood out the most and it  was kind of interesting to look at the  possibilities with that name so really  excited about you know the fact that we  are really starting a new chapter you  know we're turning a page we're going  forward we're trying to step away from  all the things that have happened in the  past but we're also at the same time i  want to make sure we honor and we honor  what has happened with this football  team in terms of the world championships  and super bowls that they've won  ron what does commanders mean to you and  you know there was a lot of pushback  since you when you announced that you  were going to change the name a lot of  pushback about changing it to begin with  what do you say to the people that are  still as the kids that today say feel in  some kind of way that you made the name  change what's your message to them and  what does commanders mean to you  well you know initially i was one of  those people that because i grew up back  in the day when when when being known as  the washington redskins was you know  what everybody knew and so i was a  [ __ ] fan  i apologize for saying um but when we  started talking about the commanders my  first thought was about leaders you know  and in today's world we seem to have a  lack of true leadership and we need  people to step forward and lead this  country and really help to take us in  the right direction i think it's greater  than just the name of a football team as  much as it's really just something that  we have to look and say you know it's an  opportunity for us to take charge take  command and go forward hey coach how you  doing nate burleson here good to see you  i hope the family is doing well um  you mentioned words like leadership and  culture and you talked about changing  that culture what exactly do you mean  and how do you plan on doing that  well i think the biggest thing about  going forward first of all  congratulations on where you are today  man you're a great inspiration to a lot  of us thank you um is that perfect you  know you're welcome going forward is so  important and and one of the things that  we've done and we've worked on it in in  washington and we've done it  purposefully and and jason wright has  done a tremendous job helping us go in  that direction that is you know we're  trying to be inclusive we're trying to  involve everybody this is not just about  a certain group of people this is about  everybody and i think that's probably  the most important thing you know we  talk about trying to develop a  sustainable winning culture and and you  have to do that by doing what's right  and doing things that you know need to  be done changing the things that need to  be changed and you know in this world  that that's important i mean we've got  to adapt and keep going forward  and not really be judged on what  happened in the past but really about  what we're doing now and what we're  going to do in the future  uh hey coach rivera it's tonya koppel  here uh on the subject of change and  leadership i've got to mention that we  we sat down with brian flores a former  head coach of the dolphins uh earlier  today he's got this new lawsuit alleging  that the league has a pattern of bias  against uh coaches of color i don't  expect you to know all the details of  the lawsuit but does he have a point in  that broader allegation that black  coaches in particular don't get a fair  shake in the league  you know i think there is something to  be looked at that really i think what  brian's doing is really really a brave  thing because again in in this world in  this you know in in what we do we've got  to be willing to open up our eyes and  really decide on merit and you know when  you look at a guy like brian and what  he's accomplished and what he's done  there's a lot of merit there and those  are the types of things that people  should be judged on and things should be  based on and i think that you know if we  really take a step back and look at it  we would we would honestly say there are  some things that we have to look even  deeper into and we've got to make sure  we make the right type of changes so  that things are inclusive that we are  doing the things that are that are right  for us  do you think coach that he still has a  chance at getting a job in the nfl after  following this lawsuit some people are  saying he just committed career suicide  what do you think on that on that score  you know  i hope he he he does because again if  you took what he's accomplished you take  his resume and you put it down on paper  and then you compare it to some of the  other candidates that are going to be  out there that's a pretty impressive  resume and i'm you know i grew up in the  military my father was an army officer  and so you know i grew up under the  guise that people were judged on merit  they're judged on rank and you got your  rank based on what you've done in the  positive things and that's kind of why  i've always looked at it um you know and  when we made some of the hires we made  when i first got to washington you know  i hired jennifer king um you know she  became the first black woman uh to to to  hold a position in the nfl on a coaching  staff and i did it because i knew who  jennifer was i understood just exactly  what she wanted and she got it to me  based on her merit i didn't do this as  as a as a stunt i did this legitimately  because i thought she was somebody who  deserved the opportunity  because of all the internships she had  done with me the work she did when she  went and she was working on a college  football team she did the things you  needed to do and so i think if you judge  people based on those things you're  going to make the right decision  coach you have been in and around this  league for a long time i have to say  this before we get off air um you are  truly truly a great coach but you're an  even better man and i appreciate you  leading the way in so many aspects real  quick tom brady's retiring what comes to  mind  oh thank goodness  you know he really is one of the  all-time greats and and then i i think  he's a guy that you know will go down as  as what they say the goat um he deserves  it but you know it is it's kind of a sad  thing for us in this league at the same  time because he's done so many great  things it brought a lot of joy to a lot  of people um and i think that's why you  play the game is to to try to be the  best and when you get to be the best you  get to go out on your terms and that's  what he's doing so congratulations to  tom brady and coach you know like i said  bengals or rams  bengals or rams  oh wow you know what um the commanders  we'll be right back give us an  opportunity  what did he say i don't know  we're gonna get shut off

